 ### Diegetic Interactor (`DiegeticInteractorComponent.h`)
 - **Aim** (`UpdateAim`, before the engine's tick, handed over as the **Custom** hit - `InteractionSource = Custom`): ray from **Camera** (the player's view point - TPS-safe), **Mouse Cursor**, or **This Component** (forward axis; VR hands). Flat Diegetic Screens by **ray-plane intersection** (no collision needed; one-sided ones only from the front (+X face); inside `[0, CurrentDrawSize]` via `GetLocalHitLocation`), curved ones by `LineTraceComponent`. Reach measured **from the pawn** (Camera / Mouse) - the screen's Reach Distance or Interaction Distance. One `LineTraceSingleByChannel` (Trace Channel; ignoring the pawn and the found screen's own actor) for occlusion, and - with **Aim At Widget Components** - plain Widget Components hit by collision (the engine computes their local hit). The used screen (Focus View) is the only candidate while in use, unlimited reach, no occlusion.
 - **After the engine's tick** (`UpdateAimedState`): `GetHoveredWidgetComponent` changes -> `NotifyAimed` on screens, `OnAimedScreenChanged`; the screen's pointer position (`Get2DHitLocation`).
-- **Presses:** `PressScreenPointer` / `ReleaseScreenPointer` (Blueprint) count on the screen (`NotePointerButton`: left/right presses, right releases, positions; the screen the press started on hears the release) and forward to `PressPointerKey` / `ReleasePointerKey`. **Click Screen** = enter Focus View on a Focus View screen not in use, else the left button. Back -> `OnScreenBack`, else `EndUsing`. Accept (in use) -> `Virtual_Accept` key down/up to the virtual user's focus. Navigate -> D-pad key press+release (Slate navigation moves the virtual user's focus), held = repeat after 0.4 s every 0.12 s. Scroll -> `ScrollWheel` (wheel: notches; stick: Stick Scroll Speed x tilt x delta).
+- **Presses:** `PressScreenPointer` / `ReleaseScreenPointer` (Blueprint) count on the screen (`NotePointerButton`: left/right presses, right releases, positions; the screen the press started on hears the release) and forward to `PressPointerKey` / `ReleasePointerKey`. **Click Screen** = enter Focus View on a Focus View screen not in use, else the left button. Back -> `OnScreenBack`, else `EndUsing`. Accept (in use) -> `Enter` key down/up (Slate's Accept) to the virtual user's focus. Navigate -> D-pad key press+release (Slate navigation moves the virtual user's focus), held = repeat after 0.4 s every 0.12 s. Scroll -> `ScrollWheel` (wheel: notches; stick: Stick Scroll Speed x tilt x delta).
 - **Input:** Enhanced Input when the player has it (`UEnhancedPlayerInput`): an `UEnhancedInputComponent` of its own pushed on the controller's stack, and two mapping contexts at **Input Priority** (100): **Aim** (Click, Secondary Click, Scroll) only while over something interactable / focusable on a widget component, at a Focus View screen, or holding a click; **Use** (Back, Accept, Navigate x4, Scroll Stick; priority + 1) while a screen is in use - their actions consume their keys (so a click on a screen button doesn't fire a weapon; Escape doesn't open the pause menu while in use). `bIgnoreAllPressedKeysUntilRelease` (Enhanced Input's default) stops a held trigger swept onto a button from clicking it. Project overrides: Aim Input / Use Input + the actions (Advanced). Unset: made once (transient) from **Default Keys** (settings): Click LMB / Gamepad Left Face; Secondary RMB; Scroll Mouse Wheel Axis; Scroll Stick Gamepad Right Y (dead zone); Back Escape / Backspace (Escape stops PIE in the editor) / Gamepad Right Face; Accept Gamepad Bottom Face / Enter; Navigate D-pad / left stick directions / arrows. Old input system: the Default Keys polled (`WasInputKeyJustPressed`) while there is something to act on (can't consume them).
-- **Focus View** (`BeginUsing` / `EndUsing`): releases held pointers; Block Pawn Input (`SetIgnoreMoveInput` / `SetIgnoreLookInput`, balanced); Show Mouse Cursor (`bShowMouseCursor`, `FInputModeGameAndUI` without cursor hiding or lock; restored to the previous cursor state, `FInputModeGameOnly` when it was hidden); a transient `ACameraActor` attached to the screen at `ComputeFocusViewTransform` (centre + face x distance so the screen fills View Fill of the view across or up, from the player's FOV and viewport aspect; + Camera Offset), `SetViewTargetWithBlend` (cubic) and back to the previous view target (pawn when none), destroyed after the blend; gamepad focus to the root widget's `GetDesiredFocusTarget` or the first widget that supports keyboard focus (`SetFocus`). In use with the cursor shown the aim follows the cursor; without it (gamepad) there is no pointer, focus drives it. `GetUsedScreen`, `OnUseBegin` / `OnUseEnd`, the screen's `SetUserInteractor`.
